# Every line names its cause: what writes the path under the root.

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The Go binary; `make build` writes it, `daisy install` links ~/bin/daisy to it
bin/

# Secrets: `daisy check-secrets` reads the workspace's .env.sh, and the root
# can itself be a workspace (below)
.env.sh

# What Daisy writes when the root is itself bound as a workspace, whatever
# the home: `daisy init` (the binding, its stage and set-aside names, the
# agent files, every skill's copies in .claude/skills and Codex's
# .agents/skills, and their Cursor stubs) and `daisy plan new` (PLAN.md,
# <slug>_PLAN.md with --spec). Whole directories, under this comment rather
# than init's header: init adds no line git already ignores here, so it
# writes no block into this file, and clean finds none to strip.
.daisy/
.daisy.stage.*
.daisy.previous.*
PLAN.md
*_PLAN.md
.claude/skills/
.claude/commands/daisy.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.agents/skills/
.cursor/rules/
.cursorignore
